<title>FINLAND: Konecranes up sharply on 96 earnings.</title>
<headline>Konecranes up sharply on 96 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish crane maker KCI Konecranes International Oy rose sharply on Wednesday after the company reported higher-than-expected 1996 earnings, brokers and equities analysts said.</p>
<p>At 1105/0955 GMT Konecranes traded at 178.00 markka, up 16.00 markka or about 10 percent, in six million markka trade.</p>
<p>Konecranes reported a 54 percent rise in its 1996 profit after financial items to 208.2 million markka, above the highest forecast of 200 million markka in a Reuters poll.</p>
<p>--John Acher, Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
</text>
